1. Update `/etc`.
2. Reduce memory to 512 MB.
3. Run `pip3 install nanobind`.
4. Run `pip3 install pytest`.
5. Add `export TZ="CET-1CEST,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3"` to `/etc/profile`.
6. Add user `pp` with password `pp` -> hardware access. Treat this account as privileged/root-equivalent: direct PulsePins hardware access can expose `/dev/mem` and DMA-backed physical memory operations.
